Subject: [PATCH] Refill the bit buffer before reading AC extra bits

JPEGDecodeMCU refills the bit buffer at the top of the AC loop, which leaves
at least 17 unread bits, and then reads a Huffman code and its SSSS extra bits
with no refill in between. When the code length plus SSSS is over 17, the
extra bits run off the end of the loaded word: the low bits come in as zeros,
the coefficient is wrong, and the bit offset still moves the right amount, so
the stream stays in sync and nothing reports an error.

The Annex K luminance AC table already has such codes: symbol 0x08 is 10 bits
long (10 + 8 = 18), and 0x09 and 0x0A are 16 bits long. High-quality files
(quantizers 1-2) put large AC coefficients on every hard edge, so text and
line art come out with smeared edges: up to 70-95 levels off libjpeg on the
gray test images in test/epubs/test_jpeg_images.epub. The fix refills before
the extra bits, the same check the DC path already makes.

---
diff --git a/src/jpeg.inl b/src/jpeg.inl
index 0b00da5..9d43513 100644
--- a/src/jpeg.inl
+++ b/src/jpeg.inl
@@ -2261,6 +2261,12 @@ static int JPEGDecodeMCU(JPEGIMAGE *pJPEG, int iMCU, int *iDCPredictor)
             usHuff &= 0xf; // get (SSSS) - extra length
             if (pZig < pEnd2 && usHuff)
             {
+                if (ulBitOff > (REGISTER_WIDTH - 17)) // a long code can leave fewer bits than SSSS
+                {
+                    pBuf += (ulBitOff >> 3);
+                    ulBitOff &= 7;
+                    ulBits = MOTOLONG(pBuf);
+                }
                 ulCode = ulBits << ulBitOff;
                 ulTemp = ~(my_ulong) (((my_long) ulCode) >> (REGISTER_WIDTH-1)); // slide sign bit across other 63 bits
                 ulCode >>= (REGISTER_WIDTH - usHuff);
@@ -2307,6 +2313,12 @@ static int JPEGDecodeMCU(JPEGIMAGE *pJPEG, int iMCU, int *iDCPredictor)
             usHuff &= 0xf; // get (SSSS) - extra length
             if (pZig < pEnd2 && usHuff)
             {
+                if (ulBitOff > (REGISTER_WIDTH - 17)) // a long code can leave fewer bits than SSSS
+                {
+                    pBuf += (ulBitOff >> 3);
+                    ulBitOff &= 7;
+                    ulBits = MOTOLONG(pBuf);
+                }
                 ulCode = ulBits << ulBitOff;
                 ulTemp = ~(my_ulong) (((my_long) ulCode) >> (REGISTER_WIDTH-1)); // slide sign bit across other 63 bits
                 ulCode >>= (REGISTER_WIDTH - usHuff);
